# policy.src - what a read directive does to the player's settings.
#   act | object | knob | weight
# act and object are concepts (isa is followed, so stab, which isa attack,
# also meets the attack rules unless a more exact rule names it). An empty
# object means the act with no object the rules know. The most exact rule
# for an act+object pair wins: exact act and object, then exact act with any
# object, then the act's parents. Not in front of the act flips the weight;
# the force words (always, should, may) scale it. Knobs run 0 to 1, from 0.5.
#
# --- attacking ---
attack||aggression|0.35
attack|power|aggression|0.3
attack|enemy-power|aggression|0.3
attack|neighbour|aggression|0.35
attack|centre|expand|0.35
attack|neutral|expand|0.45
attack|home|aggression|0.3
attack|ally-power|stab|0.5
attack|leader|balance|0.5
attack|weakest|bully|0.5
attack|distant|aggression|0.2
betray||stab|0.5
betray|ally-power|stab|0.5
betray|leader|balance|0.3
punish||retaliate|0.5
punish|others|retaliate|0.5
